{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST be the home of drafting, reviewing, and agreeing requirements, the requirement review criteria, the procedure for choosing references, and the criteria the assessment applies to code and tests.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.cli.skill_structure.requirements` says the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST be the home of six topics: drafting, reviewing and agreeing requirements, the requirement review criteria, the procedure for choosing references, and the criteria the assessment applies to code and tests. Under the parent `requirements.cli.skill_structure`, each topic is stated in full in exactly one skill.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_is_home_of_drafting_review_references_and_criteria]` is marked `{test}` and covers each obligation:\n- **Drafting, reviewing, agreeing:** it asserts that the `habeas-requirements` Workflow steps (via `workflow_steps`) contain \"Draft. Write drafts\", \"Review. Sort the new and changed requirements\" and \"**Gate:**\".\n- **Choosing references:** it asserts that the `## Choosing references` section contains \"A *root* is\".\n- **Criteria applied to code and tests:** it asserts that the `## What the review checks` section covers tests (\"obligations, boundaries, and failure cases no test runs and asserts\") and code (\"The supervising agent must still check that the code fulfills each applicable requirement\").\n- **Requirement review criteria:** it asserts that the `## Criteria` section of `references/review-prompt.md` contains the **Compound**, **Checkable** and **One reading** criteria. That file is part of the skill under the parent's definition.\n- **Exactly one home:** `assert_home(\"habeas-requirements\")` requires the skill (`SKILL.md` plus references) to contain every home marker. The markers include the drafting, subagent-review, gate, root, \"What the review checks\", \"# Requirement group review\" and \"**Compound:**\" phrases. It also asserts that none of the other four bundled skills (listed in `SKILLS`) contains any of those markers. That checks the topics are not restated elsewhere.\n\nThe assertions check the required outcome (presence in the home and absence from the other skills). A real failure would trip them, for example the topic moving out of the skill or being duplicated in another skill. I found no unmarked relevant tests and no untested obligation.",
  "references": "f159a23beb16749e13e1d1de7c5be2c78dd6bcfcbb8168129bbd0ec2bacc21bf",
  "inputs": [
